From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] fsck_hfs: report to FSKit only with FSKit's private headers

fsck_hfs.c and fsck_messages.c take their FSKit path (progress reports
through FSKitCheckStart/Update/Done) when <FSKit/FSKit.h> exists, but the
path includes <FSKit/FSKitCFunctions_private.h>, which is only in Apple's
internal SDK. The public macOS SDK has FSKit.framework, so the check passes
and the build stops. Test for the private header the path uses; without it
fsck_hfs reports progress as on a system without FSKit.

Rebase-risk: low (two preprocessor conditions).
---
diff --git a/fsck_hfs/fsck_hfs.c b/fsck_hfs/fsck_hfs.c
--- a/fsck_hfs/fsck_hfs.c
+++ b/fsck_hfs/fsck_hfs.c
@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@
 #include "fsck_hfs.h"
 #include "fsck_messages.h"
 
-#if __has_include(<FSKit/FSKit.h>)
+#if __has_include(<FSKit/FSKitCFunctions_private.h>)
 #define HAS_FSKIT
 #endif
 
diff --git a/fsck_hfs/fsck_messages.c b/fsck_hfs/fsck_messages.c
--- a/fsck_hfs/fsck_messages.c
+++ b/fsck_hfs/fsck_messages.c
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@
 #include <assert.h>
 #include <Block.h>
 #include <sys/param.h>
-#if __has_include(<FSKit/FSKit.h>)
+#if __has_include(<FSKit/FSKitCFunctions_private.h>)
 #define HAS_FSKIT
 #include <FSKit/FSKitCFunctions_private.h>
 #include <os/variant_private.h>
